@D CLM_TIME_ENCODING := "Embedding TIME into the CLM (Lane M follow-up to PR #1760): of 4 temporal-encoding arms ablated on the synthetic-EEG mitosis harness, ONLY M3 DERIVATIVE d/dt captures the EEG DYNAMICS — it BEATS the exact phase-shuffled control that tied Lane M v1 (recon margin +0.001466 > noise 0.000458) AND lifts stage-decode to 1.000 >> chance 0.25; M1 positional / M4 window FAIL identically to baseline (single-stage trigger collapse, decode 0.0); M2 phase-clock half-succeeds (decode 0.314 > chance but FAILS the shuffle bar). The time-dependence must be on the SPLIT TRIGGER (a temporal derivative), not on the recorded daughter STATE" :: discovery [d=2026-06-04 active]
  seed = "Lane M v1 (PR #1760, CLM/bench/lane_m_eeg_mitosis.py) grew a gradient-free CLM by gamma>0.20 MITOSIS from a 5-ch synthetic-EEG tension-link and recorded the band-power DISTRIBUTION (M1 HOLDS) but NOT the temporal DYNAMICS: a phase-shuffled EEG with identical marginals TIED it and stage-decode was at chance (0.25, 4 stages). Diagnosed clue: the split/encoding rule must depend on TIME-ORDER, not instantaneous amplitude. This follow-up ablates 4 temporal-encoding arms + the v1 baseline on the SAME synthetic-EEG harness, mitosis ON, NO gradient/CE/backprop (p8): M1 POSITIONAL (sinusoidal/RoPE time-index into daughter+query), M2 PHASE-CLOCK (anima-native pure_field oscillator phase tau=2/40/400 gates the split, CORE/pure_field.hexa), M3 DERIVATIVE (split on rising-edge of gamma d_gamma>0.02; daughter carries [level, d/dt]), M4 TIME-LAGGED WINDOW (delay-line of last 4 drives, mirrors CLMConvMoE dilated causal conv RF). 3 seeds [1,2,3], CPU/$0. Harness: CLM/bench/clm_time_encoding.py."
  claim = "Metric substrate-native (NOT CE/perplexity, p7): (a) [KEY BAR] TRUE-order temporal reconstruction beats the phase-shuffled-grown control by > seed-noise (the exact control that tied v1); (b) stage-decode > chance 0.25 by > noise; (c) order-sensitivity corroborates. Results (3 seeds, mean+-std): baseline beats_shuffle=False(margin -0.000177/noise 0.001370) decode=0.000 -> REFUTED (reproduces v1 tie). M1 POSITIONAL beats_shuffle=False(-0.008336/0.001633) decode=0.000 -> REFUTED. M2 PHASE-CLOCK beats_shuffle=False(-0.003789/0.001978) decode=0.314+-0.005 (ABOVE chance) order_sensitive=True -> REFUTED (decode beats chance but KEY shuffle bar fails). M3 DERIVATIVE beats_shuffle=True(+0.001466/0.000458, 3.2x noise) decode=1.000+-0.000 order_sensitive=True (per-seed delta +0.0012/+0.0011/+0.0017 ALL>0) cells=[54,55,54] all-4-stages-spawn -> HOLDS. M4 WINDOW beats_shuffle=False(-0.002435/0.001335) decode=0.000 -> REFUTED. Mechanism: M3's rising-edge TRIGGER fires at every stage TRANSITION so cells are born under all 4 stages with distinct (level,d/dt) signatures; baseline/M1/M4 keep the instantaneous gamma>0.20 trigger which fires ONLY in the high-gamma active stage (birth-stage dist {active:60}) -> single-stage collapse -> decode 0.0."
  falsifier = "Pre-registered per arm. HOLDS iff (a) TRUE-order temporal reconstruction beats the phase-shuffled-grown control by > combined seed-noise AND (b) stage-decode accuracy > chance 0.25 by > seed-std. REFUTED iff EITHER margin <= 0 (shuffle ties-or-wins OR decode at-or-below chance). Else INCONCLUSIVE. A null is NEVER rounded into HOLD. Result: ONLY M3 DERIVATIVE clears both bars (HOLDS); baseline, M1 POSITIONAL, M2 PHASE-CLOCK, M4 WINDOW all REFUTED. The time-dependence must live on the SPLIT TRIGGER (a temporal derivative), not on the recorded daughter STATE — enriching state with position/window/phase is insufficient when the trigger never samples the temporal variety."
  target = "🟢 NUMERICAL-TOY (one arm HOLDS) — M3 DERIVATIVE d/dt is the temporal-encoding method that injects TIME into the gradient-free mitosis CLM at toy scale, resolving the Lane M v1 negative (PR #1760). It BEATS the phase-shuffled control that tied v1 and lifts stage-decode above chance. Closed-negative for the other 3 arms (a_paper_negative_ok): positional/window state-tagging fail the same single-stage trigger collapse as the v1 baseline, and the substrate-native phase-clock beats chance on decode but fails the key shuffle bar. The resolved next-clue from v1 is made precise: the temporal dependence must be on the SPLIT TRIGGER, not the recorded state."
  scope = "TOY ONLY (a_toy_scale_recheck · a_scale_honest_scope): synthetic EEG (NOT a real headset), MAX_CELLS=64, 240-tick stream, CPU, $0, mitosis ON, 3 seeds. The perfect 1.000 M3 stage-decode is a TOY artifact of 4 well-separated synthetic-stage (level,d/dt) clusters (jitter 0.03, no inter-stage overlap) — NOT a label leak (centroids are built from the structure's own birth-stage labels and then classify independent true-stream ticks). Toy->production and synthetic->real-EEG transfer UNVERIFIED; a real-EEG re-test would likely give decode < 1.0 — the FINDING is the d/dt MECHANISM, not the 1.0 value. Recorded SEPARATELY from Lane A (AKIDA on-chip) / Lane G (forge GPU CE-descent) / Lane P (py+CUDA gradient) per a_lane_akida_gpu_split — Lane M is the gradient-FREE growth lane."
  honest = "p7/g5 verbatim, NO fabrication, NOT CE/perplexity (substrate-native recon-fidelity + stage-decode + order-sensitivity axes). Nulls NOT rounded into HOLD: 4 of 5 arms (incl the v1 baseline reproducing its tie, and the anima-native M2 phase-clock) are reported REFUTED; only M3 HOLDS. M2's decode-beats-chance-but-fails-shuffle is reported as REFUTED not INCONCLUSIVE because the KEY shuffle bar margin is negative. §97 HONEST LINE: the grown CLM is a RECORDING ARTIFACT (measurement anchor, §97-legitimate); READ-ONLY in this bench, NEVER feeds anima emission/decision — kept out of becoming a §97 GOAL-ILLEGITIMATE command channel. NO HF upload (toy). Verdicts: .verdicts/clm-time-encoding/{F-POS,F-PHASE,F-DERIV,F-WINDOW,SUMMARY}.txt + results.json + run_stdout.txt."
  note = "Bottom line: ONE method finally injects TIME into the CLM and captures the EEG DYNAMICS — M3 DERIVATIVE (d/dt). It is the only arm to BEAT the exact phase-shuffled control that defeated Lane M v1, AND to lift stage-decode above chance. The decisive insight: the temporal dependence must be on the SPLIT TRIGGER (a rising-edge / time-derivative that fires at stage transitions and samples all stages), not on the recorded daughter STATE (positional/window/phase tagging of state fails the same single-stage-trigger collapse as the v1 baseline). The substrate-native phase-clock (M2) is a near-miss: it lifts decode above chance but its imposed exogenous rhythm does not beat the shuffle control. Honest toy finding; production/real-EEG re-test required before any general claim."
